# 30 — Canonical router rule (reference)

The actual canonical rule for this NegritaOS install lives at:

- `/Users/jackyb-cqi/repos/NegritaOS/rules/global/negritaos_router_rule.md`

For a satellite repo that does NOT vendor NegritaOS, the canonical rule must
be available at one of:

- `~/.negritaos/rules/global/negritaos_router_rule.md` (recommended)
- A symlink in the repo: `rules/global/negritaos_router_rule.md → ~/.negritaos/...`

## Why a stub + canonical split?
- The stub at `.codex/rules/negritaos-router.md` is what each client discovers
  by scanning `.codex/rules/`. It is intentionally tiny.
- The canonical file is the authoritative governance contract. Updating it once
  updates the behavior across every repo that points to it.

## Bootstrap option for global install
```bash
# one-time, on this machine
mkdir -p ~/.negritaos/rules/global
ln -s /Users/jackyb-cqi/repos/NegritaOS/rules/global/negritaos_router_rule.md \
      ~/.negritaos/rules/global/negritaos_router_rule.md
```

Then satellite repos only need the stub.
